        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: Arctic fox, extinct Himalayan ancestor\n- Places: Arctic, Himalayas\n- Peoples: Circumpolar peoples\n- Topics: seasonal camouflage, origins\n\nFacts:\n- The Arctic fox is white in winter and brown in summer.\n- The Arctic fox lives throughout the Arctic region.\n- The Arctic fox can trace its roots to an extinct animal that lived in the Himalayas.\n- “Fjällräven” is the Ediacaran name given in the chunk for the Arctic fox.\n- Circumpolar peoples originate from the Arctic region.",
